{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/682734-pathfinding","id":682734,"title":"Pathfinding","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-30T01:01:37-07:00","id":682734,"title":"Pathfinding","content":"Has the Pathfinding mechanic been taken out of werewolf 2nd edition? I can't seem to find it in the books anywhere, anymore. And it's -awfully- bloody hard for new werewolves to get into the Shadow. Starting at Harmony 9, you've got 1 die when trying to cross. 2, if you look into something shiny. So what are the mechanics by which more than one person can cross? Are there anymore? Is it not called pathfinding? I didn't see anything in reaching, but one thing about the new werewolf book -- there are hidden little gems of rules scattered here and there that often don't seem to make their way back to the relevant sections!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5309-chancetr","name":"ChanceTR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5309_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T01:15:04-07:00","id":682782,"title":"","content":"It doesn't seem so. <br /> <br /> Note that werewolf straight from the first change begin with Harmony 9. A werewolf you stat up in character creation is assumed to have been around for some time (I usually have it for a couple of months), and as a result you actually start at Harmony 7.<br /> <br /> That said, if you're starting a game at newly newly changed werewolves, I'd probably allow some sort of equipment bonus. In the book (p101) it states staring into a reflective surface gives +1, and a meditation roll could add a +1-2 dice bonus. I've personally allow Willpower expenditure as well, in my game.<br /> <br /> Also, without stressful situations (like escaping from the Pure etc) I usually run it without a dice roll - just not interesting when they're moving over when nothings happening! But for the first time, if these are truly newbies, I'd get them to roll, adds to the drama of the scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T06:48:00-07:00","id":683067,"title":"","content":"Remember, you also add the gauntlet modifier, which at a locus is +2. So at harmony 9 you're looking at 4 dice under optimal conditions. Add willpower (nothing says you can't do that) and you're up to 7 dice. <br /> <br /> So all things considered getting a single success isn't that hard at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T07:22:43-07:00","id":683087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/682734-pathfinding?p=683067#post683067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember, you also add the gauntlet modifier, which at a locus is +2. So at harmony 9 you're looking at 4 dice under optimal conditions. Add willpower (nothing says you can't do that) and you're up to 7 dice.<br /> <br /> So all things considered getting a single success isn't that hard at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> D'oh, knew I had forgotten something!<br /> <br /> All in all it's pretty likely you'll succeed most of the time, but in a suitably dramatic moment there's enough room for something interesting to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}